# Profile: Edday (FR + EN). Sources used, all consulted 2026-10-20:
# - ZoukJam, Zouk Book, EDDAY page: bouyon artist originally from Dominica, influenced by WCK and Triple Kay Band, energetic style, catchy songs with often humorous or social lyrics reflecting daily life and challenges of young people in Dominica and the Caribbean.
# - Official WCMF 2026 media release, Roseau, 19 August 2026, relayed by Variety News Group and Mailchimp Caribbean Tourism: wider lineup groups Guadeloupe names as Les Aiglons, Jean-Marc Ferdinand and Edday.
# - writeups24, 20 August 2026, and Sweet TNT Magazine, WCMF 2026 complete guide: Edday on Saturday Night 2, 24 October 2026, with Ne-Yo, Alkaline, Tabou Combo, Asa Bantan, Vghn, Trilla G, Full Blown, Extasy Band, Reo, DYP and others.
# - Shazam song pages: Bouyon All the Way, Mr. Vegas and Edday, released 26 January 2024 by MV Music, part of Bouyon All Da Way EP, songwriters including Clifford Smith and ELIEZER VANEROT; Bay kou moto la, released 24 June 2019 by Jaiye Urban; Sco pa tu manaa, released 14 November 2019 by Jaiye Urban, language French; Make it pop, Pinpin OSP and Edday, released 2 November 2023 by VGM PRODUCT; Si Manmanw te sav, Drex, Kevni and Edday; Shaka Shaka; O Se fanm la; Foreigner, Carlyn XP and Edday.
# - Soca Podcast tracklists, Podbay and Listen Notes: Dj Chimik x Edday, Changer, listed alongside Mr. Vegas X Edday, Bouyon All The Way.
# - Black Island Girl, 12 May 2025: Strictly the Best Festival, Bouyon Edition, Lotterie Farm, St. Maarten, first festival dedicated entirely to bouyon, more than 5,000 people, Edday among the featured acts with Pudaz, Reo, Trilla G and others, closing set by Mr Ridge.
# - VP Records, Peer to Peer with Emma Mathurine: Edday named among the sounds of Dominica listened to at home, with Asa Bantan, Signal Band, Triple Kay, Carlyn XP and Reo.
# No official social profile for Edday could be verified during research, so sameAs is an empty list in both languages. Origin note: sources do not agree in presentation, ZoukJam says originally from Dominica while the official festival release groups Edday with the Guadeloupe names, and this profile reports both presentations with attribution instead of choosing one as fact.

